  "functionalScope": "Four source-family reconstruction paths build exact participant DATA without overwriting source stores. Generation local, relay and retained sources each survive an actual failed prepared save, newer pending/LIVE work and a genuine older cold reopen. Both native histories, exact rooted/sealed generations, ordered local versions, relay progress and all nonempty retained packet lanes survive absent-only recovery, exclusion of an existing writer, and repeated cold recovery. Complete recovery/operation plans, both literal input archives, committed heads/files, attempted cuts and closed pending/LIVE metadata are re-admitted independently. Facade counters remain canonical observations, not ancestry clocks. Public generation asset framing is unchanged byte-for-byte against a genuine pre-refactor file. The shared packet guard remains required for both generation and independent-delivery. All prior reconstruction and source-execution laws, complete seven-client native/whole-upload preflight and bounded cancellation remain required.",
